{
  "_about": "twin_dial probe build (SPEC section 17.1, docs/twin-dial/PROBE-PROTOCOL.md): the interfaces and fields of the probe items P1..P12, ADDED to the normal build's app.json signals by tools/twin-dial/probe_build.py (a field both blocks name is declared once; the flags must agree). READ ONLY: no 'w' flag, no setter, no _methods, no _broadcasts, no KombiIF standardCCMessage / extendedCCMessage / any setter, no requestDefaultSymbols, no newCCMessage. Every 'r' has a NON-ZERO getter id and every 's' a non-zero notifier id in the car's catalogue (tools/signals/check_signals.py passes on this file alone and on the merged app.json). Keys starting with '_' are notes. config.probe turns shared/twin_probe.js on; the normal build has no config.probe.",
  "config": {
    "probe": {
      "maxLines": 60,
      "minGapMs": 1000,
      "summaryS": [
        30,
        120,
        600
      ]
    },
    "legacyProbes": false
  },
  "signals": {
